{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>There is a sick evil.</b> It is possible that חולה is from the inheritance-pattern of the binyanim [verbs] whose second root letter is not complete [i.e., hollow verbs], and the meaning is 'a sick evil,' like 'and it is a sick evil.' Or the word חולה may be on the pattern of טובה, from the verbs whose middle root letter is not complete [i.e., יחול 'it will roil' — הל״ם is a triliteral root whose middle letter drops; the form יחול derives from it]. עודנו in the first sense, that working the land is better than all wealth."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:47.785111120Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}